    "title": "List of Masters Winners by Year: Who Has Won The Most Green Jackets? - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "cubs bears bulls blackhawks The 2026 Masters Tournament ended with Rory McIlroy claiming his second-straight green jacket. Which players have won the most green jackets in history? Who has won recent Masters tournaments? Check out the golfers with the most green jackets and more as we break down the Masters winners. More: Be sure to check out Betsperts Golf to get the best golf betting data! Most Masters Green Jackets (Tiger Woods has won 5 green jackets. 2nd all-time. Rob Schumacher-USA TODAY Sports) Jack Nicklaus not only has the most major wins of all time (18), but he also is on top of Masters history with 6 green jackets. Tiger Woods is second with 5 thanks to a win back in 2019. Check out the list of golfers with the most Masters wins and green jackets. GolferWinsYearsJack Nicklaus61963, 1965, 1966, 1972, 1975, 1986Tiger Woods51997, 2001, 2002, 2005, 2019Arnold Palmer41958, 1960, 1962, 1964Jimmy Demaret31940, 1947, 1950Sam Snead31949, 1952, 1954Gary Player31961, 1974, 1978Nick Faldo31989, 1990, 1996Phil Mickelson32004, 2006, 2010Horton Smith21934, 1936Byron Nelson21937, 1942Ben Hogan21951, 1953Tom Watson21977, 1981Seve Ballesteros21980, 1983Bernhard Langer21985, 1993Ben Crenshaw21984, 1995José MarÃ­a Olazábal21994, 1999Bubba Watson22012, 2014Scottie Scheffler22022, 2024Rory McIlroy22025, 2026 Back-to-Back Green Jacket Winners (Tiger Woods won back-to-back in 2001 and 2002. Photo by: Andrew Davis Tucker / USA Today Sports) Only four golfers in the tournament history have won back-to-back Masters. Tiger Woods, Jack Nicklaus, Rory McIlroy, and Nick Faldo. Tiger Woods won in 2001 and 2002 during a dominant stretch. From 2000-02, Tiger Woods won 6 majors. Jack Nicklaus won in consecutive years in 1965 and 1966, while Nick Faldo won in 1989 and 1990. Nicklaus ruled the 1960s with 7 major championships on his way to winning the most majors ever as one of the greatest golfers ever. Rory McIlroy is the most recent to win back-to-back Masters with wins in 2025 and 2026. Recent Green Jacket Winners at the Masters Who has won the Masters in recent years? Check out the recent winners. Since 2000, there has been just one winner who shot over par, and that was Zach Johnson, who won back in 2007, shooting +1. YearWinnerScore2026Rory McIlroy-122025Rory McIlroy-112024Scottie Scheffler-112023Jon Rahm-122022Scottie Scheffler-102021Hideki Matsuyama-102020Dustin Johnson-202019Tiger Woods-132018Patrick Reed-152017Sergio GarcÃ­a-92016Danny Willett-52015Jordan Spieth-182014Bubba Watson-82013Adam Scott-92012Bubba Watson-102011Charl Schwartzel-142010Phil Mickelson-162009Ãngel Cabrera-122008Trevor Immelman-82007Zach Johnson+12006Phil Mickelson-72005Tiger Woods-122004Phil Mickelson-92003Mike Weir-72002Tiger Woods-122001Tiger Woods-162000Vijay Singh-10 Country with Most Masters Winners The United States has dominated the Masters with over 60 wins in the tournament’s history. Check out which countries have had a golfer win the tournament. CountryWinsTotal WinnersUnited States6339Spain64South Africa53England42Northern Ireland21Germany21Scotland11Wales11Fiji11Canada11Argentina11Australia11Japan11 What is the Masters Golf Tournament? The Masters is a golf tournament that was established in 1934, and it is the first of four PGA Tour major championships played each year. The tournament is played at the Augusta National Golf Club, which is located in Augusta, Georgia. Winners of the Masters are automatically invited to play in the other three major championships for the next five years. The champion of the Masters receives a “green jacket,” with the first one being handed out back in 1949 to Sam Snead. Complete List of Masters Winners Take a look at every winner in Masters history. YearWinnerScore1934Horton Smith-41935Gene Sarazen-61936Horton Smith-31937Byron Nelson-51938Henry Picard-31939Ralph Guldahl-91940Jimmy Demaret-81941Craig Wood-81942Byron Nelson-81943None—1944None—1945None—1946Herman Keiser-61947Jimmy Demaret-71948Claude Harmon-91949S